# ROOT-ANCHORED (2026-11-07): a name-based rule matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, so an unanchored `result` would also ignore
# `internal/result/` — the exact class that once dropped `internal/reports`
# from history. `internal/arch/gitignore_test.go` walks `go list ./...` and
# fails when any package directory is ignored, which is the standing guard
# for rules the buildflow-managed block below re-generates (`build/`,
# `dist/`, `vendor/` … cannot be edited here without being overwritten).
/result
/result-*
.pre-commit-config.yaml
/.devenv
/.direnv

# >>> buildflow-managed (.gitignore) >>>
# Auto-managed by buildflow. Edit outside these markers; this block is regenerated on `buildflow --fix`.

## Secrets and environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

