.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

## Logs and temporaries
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp

## Buildflow artifacts
audit-log.*
workflow-audit-log.*
.buildflow-workflow-baseline.json

## Reports and coverage
/coverage
# ROOT-ANCHORED on purpose: this ignores the tooling's generated report
# output at the repo root, never a source package. The unanchored form
# (`reports/`) silently swallowed `internal/reports/` — the Reports tab's
# projection package — so a whole package was invisible to git while every
# local build passed and the sandbox build (which only sees tracked files)
# failed with "no required module provides package".
/reports/

